WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.546 --> 00:00:07.713
- [Voiceover] M.C. Escher
has nothing on this place.

00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:11.655
Chand Baori is one of
the largest and perhaps

00:00:11.655 --> 00:00:15.102
most visually spectacular stepwells.

00:00:15.102 --> 00:00:17.685
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.792 --> 00:00:24.997
This deep, four-sided
structure is made up of 3,500

00:00:24.997 --> 00:00:28.128
Escher-esque terrace
steps that descend down

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:30.045
to a depth of 100 feet.

00:00:33.862 --> 00:00:37.780
A large temple adorns the face
dedicated to Harshat Mata,

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.197
goddess of joy and happiness.

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:45.786
You may recognize this incredible wonder.

00:00:45.786 --> 00:00:48.096
Its intricate steps have
made appearances in Hollywood

00:00:48.096 --> 00:00:51.216
films like The Fall,
The Dark Knight Rises

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:54.133
and The Best Exotic Marigold Hotel.

00:00:57.414 --> 00:01:00.029
Northwestern India,
where the stepwell lies,

00:01:00.029 --> 00:01:01.813
is extremely arid.

00:01:01.813 --> 00:01:05.080
The well was designed to conserve
as much water as possible.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.901
At the bottom of the well,
the air remains five degrees

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.963
cooler than at the surface,
making it an excellent gathering

00:01:10.963 --> 00:01:14.403
place for locals during
intense heat waves.

00:01:14.403 --> 00:01:17.070
(upbeat music)

